      "v0.3.60 removes more Kanto movement-time CPU/GC work without lowering quality: cached trainer/wanderer NPC roles, an active-mover list, cell/generation-keyed actor candidate views, zero-allocation direct-neighbor handoff, and stale pooled actor/water/route reference scrubbing",
      "v0.3.59 removes more Kanto movement-time stutter without lowering quality: reusable voxel prefetch/live/readiness buffers, dead shared-body seam-mask elimination, once-per-frame cull bounds, caller-safe mesh residency snapshots, cheap Gold palette polling, and numeric hot-path cache keys",
      "v0.3.58 reduces Kanto frame spikes without lowering visual quality: reusable low-GC render/pose/water scratch, cached neighbor transforms/ocean descriptors, visible-only future-cache preparation, and current-sector-first cooperative voxel mesh pacing",
